But the "na" does have scope over the "ki'u". The scope is:

        na ( le nu sisku cu snada ki'u le nu na'e djuno)
It is not the case that (the seeking succeeds because of not knowing)

To get your meaning with "na" you would need to use "naku" and even
have to reverse the order:

        ki'u le nu na'e djuno le nu sisku naku snada

Otherwise "na" has scope over the whole clause.

